# Manuel Nogueira Santos - Dec 2012
# Minimalist version of flappy bird, Fixed & Updated
# must get rid of those last gotos however
# if the backgrounds are to heavy for your RPi, either remove the sky gradient or use the classic FlappyBall.kbs
gosub ScreenSetup
gosub Variables

for level = 1 to 5
	# Pre-calculate mountain noise ONCE per level load
	if level = 4 then
		for bg_x = 0 to 699
			mountain_h[bg_x] = (fbm((bg_x - 100) * 0.003, 5) + 1) / 2
		next bg_x
	endif
	# Generate obstacles safely within screen bounds
	for n = 0 to 9
		obstaclehight[n] = 50 + int(rand * 150)
	next n

	# Restart point after losing a life
start:
	# End game code
	if lifes <= 0 then gosub GameOver

	# Reset bird position on death/start
	birdy = 200: dy = -1

	# Running code
	for x = 1 to 2200 step 2
		clg # Clear screen each frame
		gosub Background

		# Text displays
		color black
		font "arial",30,50
		text 50-x,50,"Level:" + level
		if level < 5 then text 2200-x,50,"Level:" + (level+1)
		if level = 5 then text 2200-x,50,"End"

		# Drawing columns & Collision
		for n = 0 to 9
			pipe_x = 400 + n * 250 - x
			pipe_w = 50
			gap_y = obstaclehight[n]
			gap_h = 110 - (level * 5) # Gaps get smaller as levels progress

			# Only draw if visible on screen
			if pipe_x > -50 and pipe_x < 600 then
				gosub TopPipe
				gosub BottomPipe
				# Hitbox Collision Detection (Bird is at X=50, Radius=10)
				if (pipe_x < 60) and (pipe_x + pipe_w > 40) then
					if (birdy - 10 < gap_y) or (birdy + 10 > gap_y + gap_h) then
						lifes = lifes - 1
						gosub FlappyBallDead
						refresh
						pause 1
						goto start
					end if
				end if
			end if
		next n
		gosub FlappyBallAlive

		# UI Text
		color black
		font "arial",14,100
		text 10,10,"Lives: " + lifes
		text 500,10,"Level: " + level

		# Physics
		birdy = birdy + dy
		dy = dy + 0.25 # Gravity

		# Floor/Ceiling death conditions
		if birdy > 395 or birdy < 5 then
			gosub FlappyBallDead
			refresh
			pause 1
			lifes = lifes - 1
			goto start
		end if

		# Input Handling (Click anywhere to Jump)
		if clickb > 0 then
			dy = -4.5 # Flap impulse
		end if
		clickclear # Clear click buffer
		refresh
		pause 0.01
	next x
next level

# Win condition
clg
color red
rect 0,0,600,400
color black
font "arial",50,50
text 50,150,"You Win!"
refresh
end

#Lose Condition
GameOver:
color red
rect 0,0,600,400
color black
font "arial",50,50
text 130,145,"Game Over"
font "arial",14,30
text 120,250,"press mousebutton or spacebar to restart"
refresh
a=0
while clickb = 0 and a <> 32 
  pause 0.01
  a=key
end while  
birdy=200: dy=-1: lifes=5: level=1
return

ScreenSetup:
graphsize 600,400
fastgraphics
editvisible 0
outputvisible 0
return

Variables:
Dim obstaclehight(10)
birdy=200: dy=-1: lifes=5: level=1
Dim mountain_h(700) # Array to store pre-calculated heights
return

FlappyBallAlive:
penwidth 1
color red
circle 50,birdy,10
color white
circle 52,birdy-2,3
color black
circle 53,birdy-2,2
color yellow
poly {{56,birdy+3},{63,birdy+5},{56,birdy+7}, {55,birdy+5}}
color orange
line 55,birdy+5,63,birdy+5
return

FlappyBallDead:
penwidth 1
color red
circle 50,birdy,10
color black
penwidth 2
line 51,birdy-2,54,birdy+2
line 51,birdy+2,54,birdy-2
penwidth 1
color yellow
poly {{56,birdy+3},{63,birdy+5},{56,birdy+7}, {55,birdy+5}}
color orange
line 55,birdy+5,63,birdy+5
return

TopPipe:
penwidth 1
for i = 1 to pipe_w/2
	g = i * 500 / pipe_w
	color rgb(g/2, g, g/2)
	line pipe_x+i, 0, pipe_x+i, gap_y
next i
for i = 1 to pipe_w/2
	g = 255 - (i * 255 / pipe_w)
	color rgb(g/2, g, g/2)
	line pipe_x+i+pipe_w/2, 0, pipe_x+i+pipe_w/2, gap_y
next i
return

BottomPipe:
penwidth 1
for i = 1 to pipe_w/2
	g = i * 500 / pipe_w
	color rgb(g/2, g, g/2)
	line pipe_x+i, gap_y+gap_h, pipe_x+i, 400
next i
for i = 1 to pipe_w/2
	g = 255 - (i * 255 / pipe_w)
	color rgb(g/2, g, g/2)
	line pipe_x+i+pipe_w/2, gap_y+gap_h, pipe_x+i+pipe_w/2, 400
next i
return

Background:
penwidth 1
if level = 1 then gosub CitybyDay
if level = 2 then gosub CitybyDusk
if level = 3 then gosub CitybyNight
if level = 4 then gosub MountainRange
if level = 5 then gosub SeaShore
return

# Background 3
CitybyDay:
skytop_r=120: skytop_g=190: skytop_b=255
skybot_r=205: skybot_g=230: skybot_b=255
gosub SkyGradient
color rgb(255,240,150) : circle 510,70,38
# far row: small, light
body_r=165: body_g=172: body_b=190
lit_r=255:  lit_g=240:  lit_b=170
dark_r=120: dark_g=130: dark_b=155
blockw = 46
for i = 0 to graphwidth/blockw
	idx = i
	bx = i*blockw
	bw = blockw-4
	bh = 55 + int((noise(idx*0.7)+1)*45)
	by = graphheight-bh : bseed = idx
	gosub DrawApartment
next i
# near row: bigger, darker
body_r=96: body_g=104: body_b=126
dark_r=60: dark_g=66:  dark_b=86
blockw = 72
for i = 0 to graphwidth/blockw
	idx = 100 + i
	bx = i*blockw
	bw = blockw-5
	bh = 95 + int((noise(idx*0.9)+1)*60)
	by = graphheight-bh : bseed = idx
	gosub DrawApartment
next i
return

# Background 2
CitybyDusk:
skytop_r=255: skytop_g=150: skytop_b=70
skybot_r=90:  skybot_g=60:  skybot_b=110
gosub SkyGradient
color rgb(255,220,120) : circle 120,300,46
body_r=60: body_g=45: body_b=70
lit_r=255: lit_g=200: lit_b=110
dark_r=45: dark_g=34: dark_b=55
blockw = 60
for i = 0 to graphwidth/blockw
	idx = 300 + i
	bx = i*blockw
	bw = blockw-5
	bh = 80 + int((noise(idx*0.8)+1)*70)
	by = graphheight-bh : bseed = idx
	gosub DrawApartment
next i
return

# Background 3
CitybyNight:
skytop_r=10: skytop_g=12: skytop_b=40
skybot_r=40: skybot_g=30: skybot_b=70
gosub SkyGradient
color white
for s = 0 to 40
	rect (s*79) mod graphwidth, (s*131) mod 180, 1, 1
next s
color rgb(235,235,210) : circle 505,70,34
body_r=30: body_g=36: body_b=60
lit_r=255: lit_g=236: lit_b=150
dark_r=24: dark_g=28: dark_b=48
blockw = 40
for i = 0 to graphwidth/blockw
	idx = 500 + i
	bx = i*blockw
	bw = blockw-4
	bh = 120 + int((noise(idx*1.1)+1)*90)
	by = graphheight-bh : bseed = idx
	gosub DrawApartment
next i
return
function fbm(x, octaves)
	total = 0: amplitude = 1: frequency = 1: maxvalue = 0
	for octave = 1 to octaves
		total = total + noise(x * frequency) * amplitude
		maxvalue = maxvalue + amplitude
		amplitude = amplitude * 0.5
		frequency = frequency * 2
	next octave
	return total / maxvalue
end function

# Level 4 Background (fast)
MountainRange:
color blue
rect 0,0,600,350
color yellow
circle 450,30,50
color green
rect 0,350,600,400
color darkgrey
for bg_x = 0 to 599
	h = mountain_h[bg_x]
	line bg_x, 350, bg_x, 350 - (h * 150)
next bg_x
return

# Level 5 Background (fast)
SeaShore:
color cyan
rect 0,0,600,350
color yellow
circle 450,320,50
color blue
rect 0,350,600,400
color orange
poly {{410, 350}, {490, 350}, {520, 400}, {390, 400}}
color white
poly {{195, 338}, {215, 338}, {215, 310}}
color black
poly {{200, 350}, {240, 350}, {250, 342}, {190, 342}}
penwidth 3
line 220,350,220,310
penwidth 1
return


# cityBuilder helproutines
SkyGradient:
for yy = 0 to graphheight step 10
	t = yy / graphheight
	color rgb(skytop_r+(skybot_r-skytop_r)*t, skytop_g+(skybot_g-skytop_g)*t, skytop_b+(skybot_b-skytop_b)*t)
	rect  0, yy, graphwidth, yy+10
next yy
return

DrawApartment:                 # reads bx,by,bw,bh,bseed and body_*/lit_*/dark_*
color rgb(body_r, body_g, body_b)
rect bx, by, bw, bh
ww = 5 : wh = 6 : sx = 11 : sy = 13
wrow = 0
for wy = by+6 to by+bh-wh-2 step sy
	wcol = 0
	for wx = bx+5 to bx+bw-ww-2 step sx
		if ((bseed + wcol*3 + wrow*7) mod 5) = 0 then
			color rgb(lit_r, lit_g, lit_b)
		else
			color rgb(dark_r, dark_g, dark_b)
		end if
		rect wx, wy, ww, wh
		wcol = wcol + 1
	next wx
	wrow = wrow + 1
next wy
return

